# Agent Layer 2.0

Cursor is the **primary** agent surface for this repo.

## Every round start

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `agent_tools.yaml`, `agent_layer.yaml`
2. Read `reports/current-cohort-report.json` if present; the protected pre-policy `reports/latest-agent-report.json` is historical only
3. Read `reports/tool_probe_report.json`; run `scripts/tool_probe.py` only when the scoped task explicitly owns that report write
4. Read `docs/TOOL_USAGE_POLICY.md` and `docs/AGENT_RUNBOOK.md`

## Tool planning

- Map task stage to tools in `agent_tools.yaml` (`task_stage_mapping`)
- If tool availability unknown → light read-only probe first
- Log `tools_used` / `tools_not_used` in round report

## Incremental scope

- One small AL round from `docs/AGENT_ROADMAP.md` per session when possible
- P0/P1 before P2/P3 optimizations

## End of round

- Run contract-selected targeted/read-only checks in the real tree; a full `scripts/agent_gate.py` is disposable-copy-only with no writeback
- Write `reports/current-cohort-report.json`
- Append `reports/agent_audit_log.jsonl`
- Do not ad-hoc commit/push. An approved Git-safe cohort must use the hash-bound finalizer and is not complete until fresh remote SHA verification succeeds.

## Cross-agent

Same files work for Codex — see `docs/CODEX_USAGE.md`.

Legacy governance (`governance/*.yaml`, Round 41+ docs) remains authoritative for pipeline rounds.
